 "<1>XII.</1> Miscellaneous": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Preamble": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The Adjudix code of conduct. It opens the rule book and binds every neutral acting under it. <1>About the Moral Code</1>": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Adjudix Dispute Resolution Institute is established to provide parties with a fair, efficient, and dependable alternative to litigation. A procedure is only as trustworthy as the principles that govern it. This Code therefore begins with the Moral Principles that bind the Institute, its Secretariat, and every arbitrator, mediator, and conciliator acting under it.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "These principles are not aspirations. They are binding, and every provision of this Code shall be read and applied in accordance with them.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "I": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Independence and Impartiality": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Every neutral shall be, and remain, independent of the parties and impartial between them, and shall disclose any circumstance that may give rise to doubts about either.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "II": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Equality and Fairness": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The parties shall be treated with equality, and each shall be given a full opportunity to present its case.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "III": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Party Autonomy": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The parties' agreement on procedure shall be respected, save where it conflicts with this Code's non-derogable provisions or the law.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "IV": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Proceedings, documents, and outcomes are confidential, save as the parties agree or the law requires.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "V": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Integrity": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "No neutral or member of staff shall accept any gift, favour, or communication that could compromise, or appear to compromise, their integrity.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "VI": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Competence and Diligence": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Neutrals shall be appointed for their competence in the subject matter, and shall conduct proceedings with diligence and without unnecessary delay.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "VII": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Accountability": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The Institute shall maintain a mechanism for the redress of grievances arising from any breach of these Principles.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Every neutral shall, on accepting an appointment, confirm in writing that they have read and will abide by these Principles.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "<1>Chapter I</1>Preliminary": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Short Title, Extent, and Commencement": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "This Code may be called the Adjudix Code of ADR Procedure, {0}.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "It applies to every proceeding administered by the Institute, whether the parties are in India or elsewhere, and whether the proceeding is domestic or international.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "It shall come into force on the first day of January, {0}, and shall apply to every proceeding commenced on or after that date.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Definitions and Interpretation": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "In this Code, unless the context otherwise requires —": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "“Adjudix” or “the Institute”": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "means Adjudix Dispute Resolution Institute, acting through its governing body and the Secretariat.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "“Act”": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "means the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, {0}, as amended from time to time.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "“award”": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "includes an interim award, a partial award, and an award on agreed terms.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "“Code”": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "means this Adjudix Code of ADR Procedure, {0}, including its Schedules and the Schedule of Fees.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "“electronic record”": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "has the meaning assigned to it in the Information Technology Act, {0}.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "“neutral”": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "means an arbitrator, mediator, or conciliator appointed under this Code.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "“Panel”": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "means the Professional Panel of the Institute, comprising lawyers, chartered accountants and company secretaries, engineers, and other professionals approved by the Institute.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "“party”": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "means a party to the dispute, and includes its authorised representative where the context so permits.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "“Schedule of Fees”": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "means the schedule of fees and costs published by the Institute and in force on the date of commencement of the proceeding.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "“Secretariat”": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "means the Secretariat of the Institute, which administers proceedings under this Code.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Words and expressions used but not defined in this Code have the meanings assigned to them in the Act.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Scope of Application and Exclusions": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "This Code applies where the parties have agreed, before or after a dispute has arisen, to refer the dispute to the Institute, or to resolve it under the rules of the Institute or under this Code.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "It governs arbitration, mediation, conciliation, and corporate dispute resolution administered by the Institute.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "This Code does not apply to disputes which, under the law applicable to them, are not capable of settlement by arbitration or other alternative dispute resolution.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Party Autonomy and Non-Derogable Provisions": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Subject to this Section, the parties may agree on the procedure to be followed, and the neutral shall give effect to that agreement.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The parties may not derogate from the Preamble, from the provisions of this Code on the independence and disclosure of neutrals, the equal treatment of parties, confidentiality, and fees, or from any provision of the law from which derogation is not permitted.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Where this Code and the parties' agreement are silent, the neutral may conduct the proceeding in such manner as the neutral considers appropriate, consistently with the Preamble.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Waiver of Right to Object": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "A party which knows that a provision of this Code or of the parties' agreement has not been complied with, and proceeds without stating its objection without undue delay, or within the time limit provided, shall be deemed to have waived its right to object.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "<1>Chapter II</1>Commencement of Proceedings & Pleadings": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Request for Dispute Resolution and Notice of Dispute": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "A proceeding commences on the date on which a request for its commencement is received by the Secretariat, together with the filing fee prescribed by the Schedule of Fees.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The request shall state the names and contact details of the parties, a brief description of the dispute and the relief sought, the agreement under which the dispute is referred, and any proposal on the mechanism, the number of neutrals, and the language of the proceeding.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The claimant shall serve a copy of the request on every other party.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Registration of Case and Issuance of Summons": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "On being satisfied that the request is complete and the filing fee paid, the Secretariat shall register the proceeding, assign it a case number, and issue notice to every other party.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Registration is administrative and does not determine any question of jurisdiction or of the validity of the agreement, which shall be decided by the neutral.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Response, Statement of Defence, and Counterclaims": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The respondent shall file a response to the request within fifteen days of receiving notice under the preceding Section.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The statement of claim and the statement of defence, together with any counter-claim or set-off, shall be filed within such time as the arbitral tribunal may direct.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Amendment of Pleadings and Statements": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "A party may amend or supplement its claim or defence unless the neutral considers it inappropriate to allow the amendment, having regard to the delay in making it, the prejudice to the other party, and any other relevant circumstance.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "A claim may not be amended so as to fall outside the scope of the agreement under which the dispute is referred.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Joinder of Additional Parties and Consolidation of Claims": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "An additional party may be joined where all the parties, including the additional party, consent, or where the additional party is bound by the agreement under which the dispute is referred.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "After the tribunal has been constituted, no additional party shall be joined unless the additional party accepts the constitution of the tribunal and agrees to the procedural timetable, subject to such modifications as the tribunal may direct.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The Secretariat may, on the application of a party and after hearing all parties, consolidate two or more proceedings where the parties so agree, or where the claims arise under the same agreement or under compatible agreements concerning the same transaction.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "<1>Chapter III</1>Case Management & Hearings": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Preliminary Case Management Conference (CMC)": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "As soon as practicable after constitution, the neutral shall convene a case management conference with the parties.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "At the conference, the neutral shall, after hearing the parties, settle the procedural timetable, the manner of taking evidence, the place of hearings, and any other procedural matter. The timetable, and any modification of it, shall be communicated to the Secretariat and the parties.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Procedural Timelines and Time Extensions": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The neutral and the parties shall make every effort to conduct the proceeding in an expeditious and cost-effective manner, having regard to the complexity and value of the dispute, and shall observe the timelines fixed under this Code and by the neutral. The parties undertake to comply with every procedural order of the neutral.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The neutral may extend a time limit fixed by the neutral where the circumstances justify it. A time limit fixed by the Act may be extended only as the Act permits.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The Secretariat shall monitor timelines in every proceeding and may draw the attention of the neutral and the parties to any delay.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Conduct of Hearings": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Hearings shall be held at the place fixed by the neutral after consulting the parties, which may be the premises of the Institute or any other suitable place.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The neutral shall give the parties sufficient advance notice of every hearing.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Unless the parties agree otherwise, hearings shall be held in private, and no person who is not involved in the proceeding shall be admitted without the approval of the neutral and the parties.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "If a party, having been duly notified, fails to appear at a hearing without sufficient cause, the neutral may proceed with the hearing and make an award or decision on the evidence before it.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Recording of Proceedings and Transcript Management": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The neutral may direct that a hearing be recorded or transcribed, and shall do so where the parties so agree.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "A transcript or recording shall form part of the confidential record of the proceeding and shall be made available only to the parties and the neutral.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Mediation and conciliation sessions shall not be recorded.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Interim Measures by Tribunal or Neutral Authority": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "An arbitral tribunal may, at the request of a party, order any interim measure that the tribunal may order under Section {0} of the Act, including for the preservation, interim custody, or sale of goods, securing the amount in dispute, the detention, preservation, or inspection of property, and interim injunctions.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The tribunal may require the party requesting an interim measure to provide appropriate security.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "An order under this Section is enforceable in the manner provided by Section {0}({1}) of the Act.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "An application by a party to a court for interim measures under Section {0} of the Act shall not be deemed incompatible with, or a waiver of, the agreement to refer the dispute under this Code. The party shall inform the Secretariat of any such application and of any order made on it without delay.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "<1>Chapter IV</1>Evidence & Discovery": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Disclosure and Production of Documents": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Each party shall file with its pleading the documents on which it relies.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The neutral may, on the application of a party, order the production of specific documents or categories of documents that are relevant and material to the outcome, and are in the possession or control of the other party.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The neutral may draw such inferences as are appropriate from a party's failure, without satisfactory explanation, to produce a document it has been ordered to produce.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Admissibility and Assessment of Evidence": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The neutral is not bound by the Code of Civil Procedure, {0} or the Indian Evidence Act, {1}, but shall be guided by the principles of natural justice.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The neutral shall determine the admissibility, relevance, materiality, and weight of any evidence.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Examination of Witnesses and Expert Testimony": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The evidence of a witness shall ordinarily be given by written statement, and the witness shall attend the hearing for cross-examination if the neutral so directs.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The neutral may, after consulting the parties, appoint one or more experts to report on specific issues, and the parties may present expert witnesses of their own.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Electronic Records as Evidence": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Electronic records may be relied upon as evidence. The neutral may require such certification as to the source and integrity of an electronic record as the neutral considers appropriate, guided by Section {0}B of the Indian Evidence Act, {1}.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Evidentiary Privileges and Confidentiality": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The neutral shall give effect to legal professional privilege and to any other privilege recognised by the applicable law.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Statements made, documents prepared, and proposals exchanged in mediation or conciliation shall not be admissible in any arbitral or judicial proceeding, save as the law otherwise provides.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "<1>Chapter V</1>The Arbitral Tribunal": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Number, Qualification, and Nomination of Arbitrators": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The parties may agree on the number of arbitrators, which shall not be an even number. Failing agreement, the tribunal shall consist of a sole arbitrator, unless the Secretariat, having regard to the value and complexity of the dispute, determines that it shall consist of three arbitrators.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Arbitrators shall ordinarily be appointed from the Panel, having regard to the subject matter of the dispute and the professional discipline it calls for. The parties may agree to nominate a person who is not on the Panel, subject to confirmation by the Secretariat.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Appointment Procedure by Adjudix Institute": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Where the tribunal is to consist of a sole arbitrator, the parties may jointly nominate the arbitrator within fifteen days of the registration of the proceeding, failing which the Secretariat shall appoint the arbitrator within a further fifteen days.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Where the tribunal is to consist of three arbitrators, each party shall nominate one arbitrator, and the two arbitrators so nominated shall nominate the presiding arbitrator, each within fifteen days. Where a nomination is not made in time, the Secretariat shall make the appointment.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "No agreement shall confer on one party alone the right to appoint a sole arbitrator.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Every appointment is subject to the arbitrator's written disclosure and confirmation under the following Section.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Challenge to Arbitrator Appointment and Disclosure Obligations": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Before accepting an appointment, every arbitrator shall sign a statement of acceptance, availability, impartiality, and independence, make a written disclosure in the form set out in the Sixth Schedule to the Act, and subscribe to the Preamble of this Code. The Secretariat shall communicate the disclosure to the parties and fix a time within which they may comment on it. The duty of disclosure continues throughout the proceeding.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "A person whose relationship with the parties, their counsel, or the subject matter of the dispute falls under any category in the Seventh Schedule to the Act is ineligible to be appointed, unless the parties, after the dispute has arisen, expressly waive this by an agreement in writing.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "A party may challenge an arbitrator within fifteen days of becoming aware of the constitution of the tribunal or of the circumstances giving rise to the challenge, by a written statement of reasons. Unless the arbitrator withdraws or the other party agrees to the challenge, the tribunal shall decide on it in accordance with the Act.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Termination and Replacement of Arbitrators": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The mandate of an arbitrator terminates where the arbitrator withdraws, where the parties so agree, where the arbitrator becomes unable to perform their functions or fails to act without undue delay, or on a successful challenge.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "A substitute arbitrator shall be appointed by the same procedure that applied to the arbitrator being replaced. Unless the parties agree otherwise, hearings previously held may be repeated at the discretion of the tribunal.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Competence of Arbitral Tribunal to Rule on its Jurisdiction (Competence-Competence)": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The tribunal may rule on its own jurisdiction, including on any objection with respect to the existence or validity of the arbitration agreement. For this purpose, an arbitration clause shall be treated as an agreement independent of the other terms of the contract.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "A plea that the tribunal does not have jurisdiction shall be raised not later than the submission of the statement of defence. A plea that the tribunal is exceeding the scope of its authority shall be raised as soon as the matter alleged to be beyond its authority is raised.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "<1>Chapter VI</1>Arbitral Proceedings & Awards": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Fast-Track and Expedited Arbitration Procedure": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The parties may agree in writing, before or at the time of the constitution of the tribunal, that the arbitration be conducted under the fast-track procedure in Section {0}B of the Act.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018"
}
